1
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:11,594
Earlier,

2
00:00:11,594 --> 00:00:13,763
Our ancestor settled in the forest.

3
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:15,348
We used to stay in the forest too.

4
00:00:15,807 --> 00:00:18,268
We ate a lot in the forest.

5
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:22,063
We built a roof house, we built a roof house.

6
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:24,649
We walked in search of food.

7
00:00:25,275 --> 00:00:26,693
Men lived in forests

8
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:28,695
and women would go to the village to ask for help.

9
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:30,989
We lived poor, poor and poor.

10
00:00:31,573 --> 00:00:32,449
There were no clothes, no food, nothing.

11
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:33,241
No clothes.

12
00:00:33,241 --> 00:00:34,117
Nothing.

13
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:38,663
We dug yams there and killed chickens and ate them.

14
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:42,000
After eating, we moved to another place.

15
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:43,293
We moved.

16
00:00:43,793 --> 00:00:44,544
We'd build a house and settle down.

17
00:00:44,544 --> 00:00:46,588
Then we'd build a house elsewhere and settle there.

18
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:49,674
There too, to beg,

19
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:51,885
the men would go to the forest.

20
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:53,136
The woman would live in the village...

21
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:54,512
..would go to the village to beg,

22
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:56,723
Children would stay at home.

23
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:58,975
Others would gather firewood,

24
00:00:58,975 --> 00:01:00,393
make <i>raksi</i> (alcohol), and stay at home.

25
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:01,770
We used to beg to eat.

26
00:01:02,353 --> 00:01:03,146
We ate there...after finishing the forest food,

27
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:04,230
..eating the forest food,

28
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:06,733
moved to another place...

29
00:01:07,108 --> 00:01:08,318
..woud live somewhere else.

30
00:01:09,068 --> 00:01:10,111
Would beg somewhere else.

31
00:01:10,361 --> 00:01:12,238
Would roam from village to village.

32
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:15,617
Roamed around the village...used to go to the village to beg then.

33
00:01:15,617 --> 00:01:18,620
In the forest...[we] would hunt.

34
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:19,662
Would eat.

35
00:01:19,662 --> 00:01:21,831
Slaughtered chickens and sold.

36
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:24,125
We hunted for meat and ate it.

37
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:28,505
People would go far and wide.

38
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:31,382
They'd come, looking for fire, to make fire,

39
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:35,887
they'd come home, sit...come after making fire.

40
00:01:35,887 --> 00:01:46,356
Men and women would go faraway villages to beg.

41
00:01:46,356 --> 00:01:49,526
[They would] grind [grains] and bring back.

42
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:51,402
They'd bring [grains] to grind in <i>dhenki</i> (manual mill).

43
00:01:51,402 --> 00:01:52,904
They'd grind [grains] and then cook.

44
00:01:52,904 --> 00:01:55,198
They'd make rice from paddy.

45
00:01:55,198 --> 00:01:57,784
They pounded it in a <i>dhenki</i> and brought for us to eat.

46
00:01:57,784 --> 00:02:00,119
The children would stay at home.

47
00:02:00,119 --> 00:02:01,871
[We] made firewood and <i>raksi</i> (rice spirit)

48
00:02:01,871 --> 00:02:06,501
Elderly men, elderly <i>mehaq</i>s would go to villages.

49
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:11,047
Men would come to forest, eat at might and stay.

50
00:02:11,047 --> 00:02:13,675
After eating there, they'd move to another place.

51
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:15,426
Hmm...

52
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:17,679
There used to be a log for firewood,

53
00:02:17,679 --> 00:02:20,640
In that fire heat we'd sleep,

54
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:21,724
and the corner would blacken due to fire

55
00:02:21,724 --> 00:02:22,517
No log.

56
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:23,143
Fire...

57
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:24,185
Log.

58
00:02:24,185 --> 00:02:25,144
The backs would blacken due to heat...

59
00:02:25,144 --> 00:02:28,940
blacken due to heat...

60
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:30,149
Black.

61
00:02:30,149 --> 00:02:32,110
[We'd] warm up body...

62
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:32,694
Heat...

63
00:02:32,694 --> 00:02:34,070
Would warm up body.

64
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:35,321
Hmm...ask in heat...

65
00:02:35,321 --> 00:02:36,489
(Laughing) Warm up in fire...

66
00:02:36,489 --> 00:02:37,574
Hmm...Hmm...

67
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:40,869
[We would] sit and sleep by the warm fire.

68
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:42,036
No clothes either.

69
00:02:42,036 --> 00:02:42,996
Sleeping...Hmm..

70
00:02:42,996 --> 00:02:45,665
Didn't have clothes, slept wrapped,

71
00:02:45,665 --> 00:02:48,835
Would dry up...dry up in fire.

72
00:02:48,835 --> 00:02:50,461
Would dry up in fire.

73
00:02:52,088 --> 00:02:54,132
Sleep on that side. Hmm...

74
00:02:57,343 --> 00:03:01,431
On the side of the fire slept the wife and husband,

75
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:04,684
Children slept in the middle.

76
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:06,227
It used to be very cold.

77
00:03:06,227 --> 00:03:07,520
Hmm...

78
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:08,688
It's just winter.

79
00:03:08,688 --> 00:03:09,731
Winter.

80
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:10,481
It's cold.

81
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:11,983
It becomes cold.

82
00:03:11,983 --> 00:03:16,738
[We] laid dry trees on the cold roof, made bed.

83
00:03:16,738 --> 00:03:18,656
Made bed and slept.

84
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:22,493
[We] didn't eat hoofed animals.

85
00:03:22,493 --> 00:03:28,541
Our kind [Kusunda people] didn't eat yogurt, yogurt or milk

86
00:03:28,541 --> 00:03:36,549
Yogurt, cow milk yogurt, goat milk

87
00:03:41,179 --> 00:03:46,601
They didn't eat meat...didn't eat meat of hoofed animals.

88
00:03:46,601 --> 00:03:49,646
Didn't eat meat of hoofed animals.

89
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:54,525
The Kusundas didn't eat the meat of village goats.
